  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 146,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/1BpP4/8/2P5/PP1P1PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 2 4",
   "line": [
    "Bb5+"
   ],
   "spoken": "The bishop check on b5 poses real problems at first — it forces a piece to appear on d7 and, in doing so, cuts the contact between Black's queen and the d5-pawn.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "A well-timed b5 check can sever the defence of a pawn by forcing an awkward block.",
   "plans": "Exploit the loosened d5-pawn."
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 148.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1npppp/5n2/1BpP4/8/2P5/PP1P1PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 3 5",
   "line": [
    "Nbd7"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 151,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/1BpP4/8/2P5/PP1P1PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 2 4",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 158.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1npppp/5n2/1BpP4/8/2P5/PP1P1PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 3 5",
   "line": [
    "Nbd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight to d7 is Black's correct reply — but note the point: it has severed the queen's link to the d5-pawn, and now White can build with the centre rather than grabbing prematurely.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Force the defender to block on d7, then develop against the weakened pawn.",
   "plans": "Take the centre with d4 before opening lines."
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 193,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1npppp/5n2/1BpP4/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "d4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Rather than the loosening queen sortie to f3 — which Black meets with a6 — the sound choice is the pawn to d4, taking the centre and keeping every option open.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Prefer a solid central move to a committal queen raid that invites a6 with tempo.",
   "plans": "Build the centre, then decide on c4 once lines open."
  },
